/* =============================================================================
   ONE-OFF — make 'RolePreference Eligibilities' readable in the Dataverse grid
   =============================================================================
   WHY THE NAME COLUMN IS NOT A NAME

   'RolePreference Eligibilities' has no relationship to 'RolePreference
   People'. The only thing tying a row to a person is the EmployeeID TEXT
   column. The column headed "Name" is Dataverse's PRIMARY NAME column - every
   table has one, it is just text, and the import filled it with a row counter
   (1000, 1001, ...). Nothing will ever resolve it to a person, because there is
   nothing for it to resolve against.

   So editing a person's options by hand means finding their rows by
   EmployeeID, not by name.

   -------------------------------------------------------------------------
   FINDING SOMEONE'S ROWS TODAY (no changes needed)
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------
   1. Open 'RolePreference People', search the name, note the EmployeeID.
   2. Open 'RolePreference Eligibilities', filter EmployeeID = that value.
      Each row is one option that person can rank.
   3. Add a row to give them another option (EmployeeID + RoleKey are the only
      columns the app reads); delete a row to take one away.
   4. RoleKey must match 'RolePreference Roles'.RoleKey character for character
      - see diagnose-missing-roles.powerfx if an option shows as
      "[missing role: ...]".

   -------------------------------------------------------------------------
   MAKING THE GRID READABLE (optional, run once)
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------
   This rewrites the primary Name column to "428324 - Jane Bloggs - R26" so the
   grid is searchable by name, and the default lookup/search box finds people.
   The app does not read this column, so nothing in the app changes either way.

   READ FIRST:
     - It OVERWRITES the existing values (1000, 1001, ...). Confirm those row
       numbers mean nothing to you before running it - once gone they are gone.
     - It patches every row one at a time. With ~453 rows expect it to take a
       minute or two, and leave the screen open until it finishes.
     - Run it against a backup or a dev copy first if you have one.

   To run: temporary button on any screen -> OnSelect -> paste the block below
   -> Preview -> press once -> wait for the success banner -> DELETE the button.

   Check the count you are about to touch first:
     CountRows('RolePreference Eligibilities') & " rows will be relabelled"
   ============================================================================ */

ForAll(
    'RolePreference Eligibilities' As e,
    Patch(
        'RolePreference Eligibilities',
        e,
        {
            Name: e.EmployeeID
                & " - " & Coalesce(LookUp('RolePreference People', EmployeeID = e.EmployeeID).Name, "UNKNOWN PERSON")
                & " - " & e.RoleKey
        }
    )
);
Notify("Relabelled " & CountRows('RolePreference Eligibilities') & " eligibility rows. Delete this button.", NotificationType.Success)

/* -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Rows that come out as "428324 - UNKNOWN PERSON - R26" are eligibility rows
   whose EmployeeID does not exist in People. Those people cannot use the app at
   all - they get "your account is not set up for this app yet" - so it is worth
   listing them while you are here. Temporary label:

     CountRows(
         Filter(
             'RolePreference Eligibilities' As e,
             Not IsBlank(e.EmployeeID) And IsBlank(LookUp('RolePreference People', EmployeeID = e.EmployeeID).Name)
         )
     ) & " eligibility rows have an EmployeeID that is not in People"
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
